| term | value |
|---|---:|
| within z | 0.747058824 |
| within u | 0.532096531 |
| cross mean | 0.640558069 |
| signed MMD squared | -0.001960784 |
| same-array z control | -0.252941176 |
\image(figures/wae_kernel_pairs.svg)
// result_end

\caption(The same-array control is −0.252941176, because the cross mean includes self pairs while the within estimate excludes them. This negative value is retained.)
\alttext(A two-by-two within-code kernel marks the two diagonal cells as excluded. A two-by-three cross kernel retains all six numerical cells, with each normalization stated below.)

For squared pixel cost, four target zeros against four decoder values of 0.5 contribute
4×0.25=1 per image. Averaging two such images gives 1. Adding weight 10 times MMD −0.1 gives
objective 0. This arithmetic separates the image mean from the pixel sum; dividing by 784
would change its balance against the fixed MMD coefficient.

> Native data preparation and an explicit fitting loop

The native beta-vae-assets task produces the same complete local lattice as the related
WAE source: 294 binary 28×28 circle/square images. Radius=size+2, centre=(3x+5,3y+5), circles
use inclusive Euclidean radius and squares inclusive Chebyshev radius. Residue
(x+2y+size+3shape) mod 7 assigns test 0, validation 1 and fitting 2–6. All source IDs, factor
coordinates and pixels are checked against KnownFactorLattice. Factors are provenance only;
there is no external benchmark or download in this experiment.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n      = dm::nn;
  const auto cache = dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("beta-vae-assets");
  const auto a     = n::load_npz((std::filesystem::path(cache) / "beta_vae/factors.npz").string());
  auto       find  = [&](const std::string& name) {
    for (const auto& [key, value] : a)
      if (key == name)
        return value;
    throw std::runtime_error(name);
  };
  std::print("| pool | images | pixel width | explicit prior width |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n");
  for (const std::string split : {"fit", "validation", "test"})
    std::print("| {} | {} | 784 | 4 |\n", split, find(split + "_images").size(0));
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| pool | images | pixel width | explicit prior width |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| fit | 210 | 784 | 4 |
| validation | 42 | 784 | 4 |
| test | 42 | 784 | 4 |
// result_end

\caption(The split contains 210 fit, 42 validation and42 test records. All generation and fitting inputs are obtained through the native configurable cache.)

Seed 3701 initializes eight leaves/26,036 scalars in encoder/W,b; code/W,b; decoder/W,b;
output/W,b order. The widths are 784→16 tanh→4 and 4→16 tanh→784 sigmoid. Ordinary Glorot
weights and zero biases are used. Encoder/code contain 12,628 scalars; decoder/output 13,408.
BatchOrder(210,32,3761) supplies seven batches per epoch, including an 18-row final batch.
Three epochs make 21 Adam steps with rate 0.003, moments 0.9/0.999 and epsilon 1e-8.

All Gaussian banks are explicit. A fresh local MT19937/Box–Muller stream supplies Float64
standard values, then their Float32 casts. Seeds 3719/3725/3731 fix fit/validation/test prior
banks; seed 3749 supplies twenty generation codes. Epoch e uses a separate 210-row bank with
seed 3779+e; the same row indices select image and prior rows. No image-dependent posterior
noise is drawn. A changed prior can alter MMD and gradients without changing a forward
reconstruction at fixed parameters.

Every completed epoch 1–3 is eligible. **Validation squared reconstruction cost alone**
selects the checkpoint, excluding MMD. A fresh model restores all eight leaves; this is
model restore, not optimizer-state resume. The complete source preserves all first-step
artifacts, three epoch snapshots, both Gaussian dtypes, batch history and selected outputs.
The actual forward, objective, reverse mode and Adam step remain visible inside the loop.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
namespace nn = dm::nn;
namespace ae {
void Require(bool ok, const std::string& why) {
  if (!ok)
    throw std::runtime_error(why);
}
void Near(double a, double b, double tol, const std::string& why) {
  Require(std::abs(a - b) <= tol, why);
}
nn::Tensor Find(const nn::NamedTensors& a, const std::string& name) {
  for (const auto& [key, value] : a)
    if (key == name)
      return value;
  throw std::runtime_error(name);
}
struct BetaFactorData {
  nn::Tensor images, factors, source;
};
std::vector<BetaFactorData> LoadBetaFactors(const std::filesystem::path& root) {
  const auto arrays = nn::load_npz((root / "factors.npz").string()),
             known  = nn::models::KnownFactorLattice();
  std::vector<BetaFactorData> result;
  std::set<int>               seen;
  for (const std::string split : {"fit", "validation", "test"}) {
    const int  n   = split == "fit" ? 210 : 42;
    const auto raw = Find(arrays, split + "_images"), f = Find(arrays, split + "_factors"),
               ids = Find(arrays, split + "_source_ids");
    Require(
        raw.shape() == nn::Shape{n, 28, 28, 1} && f.shape() == nn::Shape{n, 4} &&
            f.dtype() == nn::DType::Int32 && ids.shape() == nn::Shape{n} &&
            ids.dtype() == nn::DType::Int32,
        "complete lattice schema");
    const auto                canonical_ids = Find(known, split + "_source_ids").to_vector<int>();
    std::vector<std::int64_t> rows;
    for (int id : ids.to_vector<int>()) {
      auto where = std::find(canonical_ids.begin(), canonical_ids.end(), id);
      Require(
          where != canonical_ids.end() && seen.insert(id).second,
          "unique identity in correct split");
      rows.push_back(where - canonical_ids.begin());
    }
    const auto x = nn::take_rows(Find(known, split + "_images"), rows);
    Require(
        nn::equal_bits(nn::cast(raw, nn::DType::Float32), x) &&
            nn::equal_bits(f, nn::take_rows(Find(known, split + "_factors"), rows)),
        "all factor coordinates and binary pixels match the core lattice");
    result.push_back({x, f, ids});
  }
  Require(seen.size() == 294, "exhaustive lattice");
  return result;
}
void SaveFactorData(const std::filesystem::path& root, const std::vector<BetaFactorData>& pools) {
  nn::NamedTensors arrays;
  for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k) {
    const std::string s = k == 0 ? "fit" : k == 1 ? "validation" : "test";
    arrays.emplace_back(s + "_images", pools[k].images);
    arrays.emplace_back(s + "_factors", pools[k].factors);
    arrays.emplace_back(s + "_source_ids", pools[k].source);
  }
  nn::save_npz((root / "data.npz").string(), arrays);
}
nn::NamedTensors Arrays(const nn::ParameterStore& p) {
  nn::NamedTensors a;
  for (const auto& name : p.names())
    a.emplace_back(name, p.at(name).detach().clone());
  return a;
}
auto Snapshot(const nn::ParameterStore& p) {
  return p.flatten();
}
double Mse(const nn::Tensor& a, const nn::Tensor& b) {
  return nn::mean(
             nn::square(
                 nn::cast(a.reshape({a.size(0), 784}), nn::DType::Float64) -
                 nn::cast(b.reshape({b.size(0), 784}), nn::DType::Float64)))
      .item();
}
nn::Tensor PixelMean(const nn::Tensor& x) {
  return nn::cast(
      nn::mean(nn::cast(x.reshape({x.size(0), 784}), nn::DType::Float64), {0}), nn::DType::Float32);
}
nn::Tensor Constant(const nn::Tensor& row, int n) {
  return nn::broadcast_to(row.reshape({1, 784}), {n, 784}).contiguous();
}

nn::Tensor Flatten(const nn::Tensor& x) {
  return x.reshape({x.size(0), 784});
}
struct VaeNoiseBank {
  nn::Tensor standard, epsilon;
};
VaeNoiseBank BetaVaeNoise(std::int64_t n, std::int64_t samples, std::uint32_t seed) {
  const auto standard = nn::models::GaussianNoise({n, 4}, samples, seed);
  return {standard, nn::cast(standard, nn::DType::Float32)};
}
nn::Tensor BetaVaeNoiseAt(const VaeNoiseBank& bank, std::int64_t k) {
  return nn::select(bank.epsilon, 0, k).contiguous();
}
using nn::models::ImqMmd;
void Warm(nn::ParameterStore& p) {
  nn::NoGradGuard guard;
  nn::models::WassersteinAutoencoder(p, nn::zeros({2, 784}), nn::zeros({2, 4}));
}
nn::NamedTensors
Evaluate(nn::ParameterStore& p, const nn::Tensor& images, const nn::Tensor& prior) {
  nn::NoGradGuard  guard;
  const auto       n = nn::models::WassersteinAutoencoder(p, Flatten(images), prior);
  nn::NamedTensors out{
      {"code", n.code},
      {"logits", n.logits},
      {"probability", n.probability},
      {"squared_cost", n.squared_cost},
      {"reconstruction_loss", n.reconstruction_loss},
      {"mmd_xx", n.mmd.xx},
      {"mmd_yy", n.mmd.yy},
      {"mmd_xy", n.mmd.xy},
      {"mmd_within_x", n.mmd.within_x},
      {"mmd_within_y", n.mmd.within_y},
      {"mmd_cross", n.mmd.cross},
      {"mmd", n.mmd.value},
      {"loss", n.loss}};
  for (auto& [name, t] : out) {
    t = t.contiguous();
    for (double v : t.to_vector<double>())
      Require(std::isfinite(v), "all WAE endpoints finite");
  }
  return out;
}
nn::Tensor Decode(nn::ParameterStore& p, const nn::Tensor& code) {
  nn::NoGradGuard guard;
  return nn::sigmoid(nn::models::WaeDecode(p, code)).contiguous();
}
nn::NamedTensors CheckGradients(
    const nn::ParameterStore&      p,
    const std::vector<nn::Tensor>& g,
    const std::string&             finite,
    const std::string&             nonzero) {
  Require(g.size() == p.size(), "all eight derivative leaves");
  nn::NamedTensors out;
  const auto       names = p.names();
  for (std::size_t k = 0; k < g.size(); ++k) {
    double norm = 0;
    for (double x : g[k].to_vector<double>()) {
      Require(std::isfinite(x), finite);
      norm += x * x;
    }
    Require(norm > 0, nonzero);
    out.emplace_back(names[k], g[k]);
  }
  return out;
}
} // namespace ae
namespace check {
using ae::Near;
using ae::Require;
} // namespace check
namespace {

namespace nn = datamunge::nn;

double Difference(const nn::Tensor& a, const nn::Tensor& b) {
  check::Require(a.shape() == b.shape(), "matching outputs");
  const auto x = a.contiguous().to_vector<float>(), y = b.contiguous().to_vector<float>();
  double     d = 0;
  for (size_t i = 0; i < x.size(); ++i)
    d = std::max(d, std::abs(double(x[i]) - y[i]));
  return d;
}
float Scalar(const nn::NamedTensors& f, const std::string& name) {
  return ae::Find(f, name).item<float>();
}

void Algebra(const std::filesystem::path& root) {
  std::vector<float> a(12), b(16);
  for (int i = 0; i < 12; ++i)
    a[i] = .2f * (i - 5);
  for (int i = 0; i < 16; ++i)
    b[i] = .15f * ((i * 7) % 17 - 8);
  auto x            = nn::from_vector(a, {3, 4}).requires_grad_(),
       y            = nn::from_vector(b, {4, 4}).requires_grad_();
  auto            m = ae::ImqMmd(x, y);
  auto            g = nn::grad(m.value, {x, y});
  nn::NoGradGuard guard;
  auto            same = ae::ImqMmd(x, x), zero = ae::ImqMmd(nn::zeros({3, 4}), nn::zeros({4, 4}));
  check::Near(zero.value.item<float>(), 0, 0, "all-identical latent kernel yields exactzero MMD");
  check::Require(
      same.value.item<float>() < 0,
      "same finite empirical sample unbiased estimator CAN be negative,do not clip");
  const auto gx = g[0].to_vector<float>(), gy = g[1].to_vector<float>();
  for (int j = 0; j < 4; ++j) {
    double sum = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < 3; ++i)
      sum += gx[i * 4 + j];
    for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i)
      sum += gy[i * 4 + j];
    check::Near(sum, 0, 1e-6, "joint translation invariance gradient");
  }
  nn::save_npz(
      (root / "mmd_algebra.npz").string(),
      {{"x", x.detach()},
       {"y", y.detach()},
       {"xx", m.xx.detach()},
       {"yy", m.yy.detach()},
       {"xy", m.xy.detach()},
       {"mmd", m.value.detach()},
       {"gradient_x", g[0]},
       {"gradient_y", g[1]},
       {"same_sample_unbiased_mmd", same.value},
       {"all_identical_mmd", zero.value}});
}

void Run(
    const std::filesystem::path& data,
    const std::filesystem::path& root,
    int                          epochs,
    const std::string&           init) {
  auto pools = ae::LoadBetaFactors(data);
  std::filesystem::create_directories(root);
  Algebra(root);
  std::vector<ae::VaeNoiseBank> priors;
  nn::NamedTensors              bank;
  for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k) {
    const std::string split = k == 0 ? "fit" : k == 1 ? "validation" : "test";
    priors.push_back(ae::BetaVaeNoise(pools[k].images.size(0), 1, 3719 + k * 6));
    bank.emplace_back(split + "_standard", priors[k].standard);
    bank.emplace_back(split + "_epsilon", priors[k].epsilon);
  }
  auto generation = ae::BetaVaeNoise(20, 1, 3749);
  bank.emplace_back("generation_standard", generation.standard);
  bank.emplace_back("generation_epsilon", generation.epsilon);
  ae::SaveFactorData(root, pools);
  nn::save_npz((root / "fixed_noise.npz").string(), bank);
  nn::ParameterStore model(3701);
  ae::Warm(model);
  nn::OptimizerConfig config;
  config.kind = nn::OptimizerKind::Adam;
  nn::Optimizer optimizer(model, .003, config);
  if (!init.empty())
    model.load(init);
  check::Require(model.count() == 26036 && model.size() == 8, "compact deterministic WAE census");
  nn::save_npz((root / "initial_arrays.npz").string(), ae::Arrays(model));
  nn::BatchOrder order(210, 32, 3761);
  std::ofstream  history(root / "history.tsv"), batches(root / "batches.tsv");
  history.precision(17);
  history << "epoch\tvalidation_squared_cost\tvalidation_mmd\tvalidation_objective\n";
  batches << "epoch\tstep\trow\tsource_id\n";
  const auto fit_source = pools[0].source.to_vector<int>();
  const auto best_path  = (root / "best.npz").string();
  double     best       = std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity();
  int        selected = 0, steps = 0;
  const auto started = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
  for (int epoch = 1; epoch <= epochs; ++epoch) {
    auto noise = ae::BetaVaeNoise(210, 1, 3779 + epoch);
    nn::save_npz(
        (root / ("train_noise_epoch" + std::to_string(epoch) + ".npz")).string(),
        {{"standard", noise.standard}, {"epsilon", noise.epsilon}});
    auto prior = ae::BetaVaeNoiseAt(noise, 0);
    order.begin_epoch();
    int seen = 0;
    for (;;) {
      auto rows = order.next();
      if (rows.empty())
        break;
      auto x = nn::take_rows(pools[0].images, rows), p = nn::take_rows(prior, rows);
      if (steps == 0) {
        nn::save_npz((root / "first_batch.npz").string(), {{"images", x}, {"prior", p}});
        nn::save_npz((root / "first_forward.npz").string(), ae::Evaluate(model, x, p));
        nn::save_npz(
            (root / "first_gradients.npz").string(),
            ae::CheckGradients(
                model,
                nn::grad(
                    nn::models::WassersteinAutoencoder(model, ae::Flatten(x), p).loss,
                    model.parameters()),
                "all WAE derivatives finite",
                "all8tensors receive WAE gradients"));
      }
      const auto forward = nn::models::WassersteinAutoencoder(model, ae::Flatten(x), p);
      check::Require(std::isfinite(forward.loss.item<float>()), "finite signed WAE objective");
      const auto gradients = nn::grad(forward.loss, model.parameters());
      optimizer.step(gradients);
      if (steps == 0)
        nn::save_npz((root / "first_update_arrays.npz").string(), ae::Arrays(model));
      for (auto row : rows)
        batches << epoch << '\t' << steps << '\t' << row << '\t' << fit_source[row] << '\n';
      ++steps;
      seen += int(rows.size());
    }
    check::Require(seen == 210, "all fit images once per epoch");
    auto         v     = ae::Evaluate(model, pools[1].images, ae::BetaVaeNoiseAt(priors[1], 0));
    const double score = Scalar(v, "reconstruction_loss");
    history << epoch << '\t' << score << '\t' << Scalar(v, "mmd") << '\t' << Scalar(v, "loss")
            << '\n';
    nn::save_npz(
        (root / ("epoch" + std::to_string(epoch) + "_arrays.npz")).string(), ae::Arrays(model));
    if (score < best) {
      best     = score;
      selected = epoch;
      model.save(best_path); // validation squared transport cost selects WAE
    }
    std::cout << "epoch" << epoch << ":validation squaredcost=" << score
              << ",MMD=" << Scalar(v, "mmd") << ",objective=" << Scalar(v, "loss") << std::endl;
  }
  const double seconds =
      std::chrono::duration<double>(std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - started).count();
  nn::ParameterStore deployed(3701);
  ae::Warm(deployed);
  deployed.load(best_path); // fresh WAE model-only restore
  check::Near(
      Scalar(
          ae::Evaluate(deployed, pools[1].images, ae::BetaVaeNoiseAt(priors[1], 0)),
          "reconstruction_loss"),
      best,
      1e-8,
      "restored validation cost");
  const auto       before = ae::Snapshot(deployed);
  nn::NamedTensors outputs;
  for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k) {
    const std::string split = k == 0 ? "fit" : k == 1 ? "validation" : "test";
    for (const auto& [key, value] :
         ae::Evaluate(deployed, pools[k].images, ae::BetaVaeNoiseAt(priors[k], 0)))
      outputs.emplace_back(split + "_" + key, value);
  }
  auto p      = ae::BetaVaeNoiseAt(priors[2], 0);
  auto test   = ae::Evaluate(deployed, pools[2].images, p),
       repeat = ae::Evaluate(deployed, pools[2].images, p),
       other  = ae::Evaluate(
           deployed, pools[2].images, ae::BetaVaeNoiseAt(ae::BetaVaeNoise(42, 1, 3793), 0));
  const auto probability = ae::Find(test, "probability");
  check::Require(
      nn::equal_bits(probability, ae::Find(repeat, "probability")) &&
          nn::equal_bits(probability, ae::Decode(deployed, ae::Find(test, "code"))),
      "repeat/code-only decoder BITEXACT");
  check::Require(
      nn::equal_bits(ae::Find(test, "code"), ae::Find(other, "code")) &&
          !nn::equal_bits(ae::Find(test, "mmd"), ae::Find(other, "mmd")),
      "prior changes aggregate regularizer,not deterministic encoding");
  auto small =
      ae::Evaluate(deployed, nn::take_rows(pools[2].images, {0, 1}), nn::take_rows(p, {0, 1, 2}));
  const double parity =
      Difference(ae::Find(small, "probability"), nn::take_rows(probability, {0, 1}));
  check::Require(parity < 2e-6, "reconstruction small/batch parity with UNEQUAL prior count");
  bool rejected = false;
  try {
    ae::Evaluate(deployed, nn::take_rows(pools[2].images, {0}), p);
  } catch (const std::exception&) {
    rejected = true;
  }
  check::Require(rejected, "singleton unbiased MMD sample rejected before division");
  auto prior_z = ae::BetaVaeNoiseAt(generation, 0), prior = ae::Decode(deployed, prior_z);
  nn::save_npz((root / "prior.npz").string(), {{"z", prior_z}, {"probability", prior}});
  nn::save_npz((root / "model_arrays.npz").string(), ae::Arrays(deployed));
  nn::save_npz((root / "outputs.npz").string(), outputs);
  check::Require(before == ae::Snapshot(deployed), "all WAE inference immutable");
  auto         mean     = ae::Constant(ae::PixelMean(pools[0].images), 42);
  const double mse      = ae::Mse(probability, pools[2].images),
               baseline = ae::Mse(mean, pools[2].images);
  const double cost = Scalar(test, "reconstruction_loss"), mmd = Scalar(test, "mmd"),
               objective = Scalar(test, "loss");
  std::ofstream meta(root / "metrics.json");
  meta.precision(17);
  meta << "{\"parameters\":26036,\"tensors\":8,\"epochs\":" << epochs << ",\"updates\":" << steps
       << ",\"selected_epoch\":" << selected << ",\"mmd_weight\":10,\"test_squared_cost\":" << cost
       << ",\"test_mmd\":" << mmd << ",\"test_objective\":" << objective << ",\"test_mse\":" << mse
       << ",\"fit_mean_mse\":" << baseline << ",\"small_batch_max_error\":" << parity
       << ",\"training_seconds\":" << seconds << "}\n";
  check::Require(bool(meta) && bool(history) && bool(batches), "complete WAE evidence");
  std::print(
      "| selected epoch | test squared pixel sum | signed MMD | penalized objective | test MSE | "
      "fit-only mean MSE |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| {} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | "
      "{:.9f} | {:.9f} |\n",
      selected,
      cost,
      mmd,
      objective,
      mse,
      baseline);
}

} // namespace

int main() {
  try {
    const std::filesystem::path cache = dm::datasets::data_home();
    dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("beta-vae-assets", cache.string());
    Run(cache / "beta_vae", "build/wae", 3, "");
    return 0;
  } catch (const std::exception& e) {
    std::cerr << e.what() << '\n';
    return 1;
  }
}
