All eighteen archives/1,147,656 values and TSV histories match the frozen original exactly.
Only two summary MSE reductions use tensor Float64 accumulation instead of host summation;
other non-timing JSON values remain exact. The optional NumPy oracle checks the saved
Gaussian banks, every first derivative and the exact first Adam update independently.

> Reconstruction improves while aggregate matching worsens

The next two plots use epoch-end validation measurements at the same three checkpoints.
The selection score decreases, whereas the signed MMD rises. This reveals the tradeoff
in this short run; it is not evidence that the prior and encoded distributions match.
Neither curve uses held-out test records to select the model.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/wae_validation_cost.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::ifstream input("build/wae/history.tsv");
  std::string   header;
  std::getline(input, header);
  std::vector<double> e, cost, objective;
  double              epoch, c, m, l;
  while (input >> epoch >> c >> m >> l) {
    e.push_back(epoch);
    cost.push_back(c);
    objective.push_back(l);
  }
  if (e.size() != 3)
    return 1;
  auto chart = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  chart.lines(e, cost, "squared cost", dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}, 2)
      .points(e, cost, "", dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}, 5)
      .lines(e, objective, "cost +10 MMD", dm::RGBA{220, 38, 38}, 2)
      .points(e, objective, "", dm::RGBA{220, 38, 38}, 5)
      .title("Validation reconstruction cost selects epoch 3")
      .x_label("completed epoch / all three eligible")
      .y_label("mean pixel-summed squared cost / objective")
      .x_ticks({1, 2, 3}, {"1", "2", "3"})
      .save_svg("build/wae_validation_cost.svg");
}
